						<div style="width:100%;">
							<div align="center"><font face="Arial" size="3"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font size="4"><b><img src="/pics/2103/faqs.jpg" /><br />Frequently Asked Questions</b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial" size="3"> <div align="justify"><br /><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> Is soldier planning on being an alliance or horde guild? And if so what race?</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><i><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> Soldier is slated to be an Alliance guild. Though we are not a race dependent guild. A member is eligible if they are any race from the Alliance: Human, Gnome, Dwarf, Night Elf. </i></b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><i><font color="#d3d3d3" size="2"><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> </font></i></font><font face="Arial"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i>How often does the guild expect to raid once we achieve a raiding level? Until we do, will there be lower level events/mini raids?</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> </b></font><font face="Arial"><b>Soldier will be raiding in accordance with the availability of actual raid mobs in World of Warcraft, this could be every night if they're available, or every other night if there is a shortage of mobs among the community. Overall, Soldier is focused on the high end game. Though we are not going to completely powergame up to the end game, we would like to enjoy the content of the low-mid level content, but will not stay there. We will be having events and raids of the current level we can handle until we reach the high end of the game. Also, we will be making events out of any quests that might need a raid party for completion for our members.</b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><i><font color="#d3d3d3" size="2"><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> </font></i></font><font face="Arial"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i>How will the guild stand on PvP? will you be taking active roles in pvp as a guild, or only as a individual basis?</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> </b></font><font face="Arial"><b>As for PvP, Soldier is not by any means a PvP guild. We are former MMORPG Players (such as EverQuest). The guild will be focused on competing against other guilds for raid mobs and being one of the top guilds on the server and in World of Warcraft.&nbsp;Player versus player tournaments within the guild will be conducted as fun events a few times a month. This is just to better the individual skills of players in Soldier. Players are encouraged to participate in PvP in server tournaments, though this is only on an individual level.</b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><i><font color="#d3d3d3" size="2"><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> </font></i></font><font face="Arial"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i>Will&nbsp;you have a guild depository, so new members can get properly outfitted when they join? Of course, us players playing from launch will be the ones to have to fill it with no return for ourselves, but i feel they really help later on for the guild.</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> </b></font><font face="Arial"><b>A guild bank/depository, will be available to new members of the guild as soon as possible. Yes, those of us that are playing from actual retail launch will be responsible for compiling this Guild Bank. All items that will be in this depository will be guild owned and if a player leaves the guild, they will be required to give back guild owned items if the guild could still use it.</b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><i><font color="#d3d3d3" size="2"><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> </font></i></font><font face="Arial"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i>What kind of loot system will be used on raids? Will you be using a Need Before Greed system, meaning anyone who needs said item is free to roll on it.&nbsp;Will you use&nbsp;a DKP system, meaning you earn points by helping others do quests, giving out items, and raiding in general. Then use said points to bid on items that drop. Or, will the officers/raid leader decide where loot goes?</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> </b></font><font face="Arial"><b>Soldier will be using a DKP system for loot&nbsp;on raids.&nbsp;We have an automated program that not only tracks who is on a raid, but also how many DKP is earned, what mob is killed, and what items are looted. As you mentioned the DKP system, I expect that you know what it means so I won't go into detail. If a person is in dire need of a quest item, and this item is up for DKP they can bring this to the attention of the officers and the item may be given to that person on the basis of merit and need. The only items that will be DKP based are going to be major drops on raids, therefore drops/loot from mini-named will not be based on DKP and will be randomly rolled on all that want it.&nbsp; Furthermore, helping someone with a quest is not something that generated DKP from my experiences, but we will look into this in the future if quests require this much attention to award DKP for them.</b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><i><font color="#d3d3d3" size="2"><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> </font></i></font><font face="Arial"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i>What kind of server will you be on? RP, FVF, or a normal server?</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> </b></font><font face="Arial"><b>Soldier wil be based on a (regular) PvE server since we are focused on the high end game and do not want to limit our ability to get there by playing on a server that focuses mainly on roleplaying or PvP. We want to make the game as rich an experience as possible.</b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> With a name like Soldier are you going to be an all Warrior guild?</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> What?! Nah that would never work! We welcome all classes from the Alliance.</b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font>What physical location will most of the players be from?</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> Most of the players will be from the US and within that will be spread around the country from mass. to california and as south as missouri and texas. </b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><i><font color="#d3d3d3" size="2"><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> Will their be requirements that </font></i></font><font face="Arial"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i>we have to be seen like every hour of the day?</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> Absolutely not. If you're putting forth a good effort to play and be an integral part of the guild, play time is not an issue. Those of us that do play more will enjoy the benefits that come with it. </b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> Will there be punch and pie?</i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> Yes punch and pie will be provided.</b></font><br /><font face="Arial"><b>(Off topic)</b></font><br /></font></div></font><font face="Arial"> <div align="justify"><br /><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><i><font color="#ffa500">Q.</font> Where do I sign up!? </i><br /></font></div></font></font> <div align="justify"><font size="2"><font color="#d3d3d3"><font face="Arial"><b><font color="#ffff00">A.</font> You can contact Wars, or any other officer in-game. These officers are found on the&nbsp;List of Soldiers&nbsp;&nbsp;page. You can also Email me at SuperSolidSaiyan@yahoo.com . Also check out the Become a Soldier page for more information.</b></font><br /></font></div></font>
							
